redfin 1092: IOService "Baseband Voice" (coder V2, 2026-11-14). BBA study A1.
BasebandVoice.driver (mediaserverd) checks IOServiceGetMatchingService(IOServiceNameMatching("Baseband Voice")) once
when it loads; a service of that name = "BVCanPublishBasebandVoice: NO (I2S device present)", so the stock driver
stands down and our RedwoodAudio "Baseband Voice" device can own call audio. The driver reads nothing from the service
(no properties beyond SweetABP=true); IOServiceOpen on it is logged (first 8) and refused (kIOReturnUnsupported).
- Default OFF (no loader of kern.sweet_* values runs before mediaserverd: sweetctl boot-apply runs from SpringBoard).
- boot-arg sweetbbv=1: published from SweetABPStart (needs sweetabp & 1) before mediaserverd starts.
- kern.sweet_bbv_service: reads 1 when published; write 1 publishes, 0 terminates (ENXIO without sweetabp services).
  mediaserverd decides only at start: restart it after a change.

